---
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";

const title = "April 7 West Covina City Council Meeting — What Happened & What It Means";
const description = "Full breakdown of the April 7 West Covina City Council meeting including Fire Station 3 repairs, street sweeping decisions, and key financial impacts.";
---

<MainLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">

    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">
      April 7 City Council Meeting — What Actually Happened (And What It Means for West Covina)
    </h1>

    <p class="mb-6 text-gray-600">
      I went through the full April 7th City Council meeting—start to finish—and broke down what actually matters.
    </p>

    <img 
      src="/images/april-7-city-council.jpg" 
      alt="West Covina City Council meeting breakdown"
      class="w-full rounded-lg mb-8"
    />

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-2">The Meeting at a Glance</h2>
    <p>
      On the surface, the meeting looked routine. But underneath were three major decisions:
    </p>

    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6">
      <li>Fire Station 3 emergency repairs</li>
      <li>Street sweeping program changes</li>
      <li>Financial decisions tied to past planning</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-2">Fire Station 3</h2>
    <p>
      The city approved emergency repairs after a long-standing issue escalated into unsafe conditions.
      This highlights a larger pattern of reactive maintenance.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-2">Street Sweeping</h2>
    <p>
      A 3–2 vote kept the current system, but added enforcement and monitoring. This is not a final decision—
      it’s an evolving rollout.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-2">The Bigger Pattern</h2>
    <p>
      Across decisions, the same pattern shows up: reactive systems, open-ended plans, and incremental changes.
    </p>

    <hr class="my-10" />

    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
      Full detailed breakdown available on Substack:
      <a 
        href="https://open.substack.com/pub/justinpresswc/p/west-covina-city-council-meeting-63a?utm_source=stayjustin&utm_medium=site"
        class="text-blue-600 underline"
        target="_blank"
      >
        Read full article
      </a>
    </p>

  </section>
</MainLayout>
